import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a5 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Backend video editing runtime","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/server-video-editor/spec.md","filePath":"feature/server-video-editor/spec.md"}'),r={name:"feature/server-video-editor/spec.md"};function s(n,e,d,l,c,u){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="backend-video-editing-runtime" tabindex="-1">Backend video editing runtime <a class="header-anchor" href="#backend-video-editing-runtime" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Backend video editing runtime&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="objective-and-authorization" tabindex="-1">Objective and authorization <a class="header-anchor" href="#objective-and-authorization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Objective and authorization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>User asks to move the complete usable DemoVideo/Viro editing workflow into backend, so the web accepts simple instructions and returns a finished video from a worker deployable on a VM. User additionally confirmed existing video and narration uploads, alongside image+prompt. Preserve the sources at F:/self, existing manual editor, and all unrelated changes. No commit/push or VM purchase/deployment. Existing instruction to use BrandHub credits and review costs before paid video generation remains; this feature must not silently generate new paid footage.</p><h2 id="observable-acceptance" tabindex="-1">Observable acceptance <a class="header-anchor" href="#observable-acceptance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Observable acceptance&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>In Video Space, users may import video/image/audio using existing media import and ask for an automatic server edit. Canonical saved project/media are the input, not client object URLs, paths or credentials.</li><li>Workflow includes source verification/probe, frame/voice analysis, genre-based editorial plan, real rendering, sound mix/subtitles/graphics, decode/timing QC, private output storage, progress/error/result download. Original timeline/media are not overwritten.</li><li>Existing 8-action assistant remains; a separate server-render action produces an MP4. Server render does not require the user&#39;s browser to remain open.</li><li>Support clips/stills, trim/retime, freeze, crop/blur background, restrained zoom, transitions, captions/title/score cards, circle/arrow callouts, supplied alpha-portrait glow/compositing, provided voice, music/SFX and measured final audio. Use provided facts/transcript; never invent events, speech, product claims or missing source media. Do not claim object tracking or automatic background removal if no implementation exists.</li><li>Include complete first-party DemoVideo guide/reference/genre library and reusable first-party tools with provenance. Preserve individual licenses/notices; SeeCut Noncommercial runtime is not included in commercial execution. Include CC0/public-domain SFX and existing OFL font/original music. No hardcoded personal paths, Windows fonts or sports footage as general input.</li><li>Speech: supplied voice may be transcribed by installed faster-whisper with explicitly available/mounted model; verified user transcript may be used. Optional configured TTS can generate narration. Missing dependencies/model/provider fail explicitly, never silent fake captions or substitute samples. No automatic model download in a request. Whole-skill documentation is not claimed as whole-skill executable support: readiness lists each tool/capability.</li><li>Produce at least one real offline synthetic fixture with voice/audio, portrait overlay, freeze/callout, captions and transitions. Inspect final duration, decoded frames/pixels and audio. Compare techniques with Nyambe r06 (43.7s,1080x1920,30fps); no promise of matching aesthetics without review.</li></ol><h2 id="architecture-contract" tabindex="-1">Architecture contract <a class="header-anchor" href="#architecture-contract" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Architecture contract&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Business owns auth/owner/workspace, canonical private asset descriptors, idempotency and current credit policy. AI/worker owns typed editorial plan, analysis/render/QC. Reuse existing internal key and storage credentials; no keys in frame/browser. Dedicated worker API can run locally or on Linux VM without importing crawl/NLP app startup. Existing API proxies internal planning to worker, allowing current credit generation service to account for the Claude planning call. Rendering reuses paid planning receipt, does not invent a new free credit operation or auto-pay for new footage.</p><p>Public endpoints under <code>/api/v1/workspaces/{ws}/video-projects/{project}</code>:</p><ul><li><code>POST /auto-edits</code> with mandatory Idempotency-Key, body <code>{expected_revision,instruction}</code> (revision&gt;=1, instruction1..4000). Canonical owner snapshot/assets only. Response202 <code>ApiResponse&lt;{id,status,stage,base_revision,...}&gt;</code>.</li><li><code>GET /auto-edits/{job}</code>: owner-scoped progress and output metadata, no storage keys/signed URLs.</li><li><code>GET /auto-edits/{job}/content</code>: authorized private MP4 streaming after COMPLETED, no regeneration/provider refresh. Error leaves originals intact.</li></ul><p>Internal worker API base <code>/api/v1/ai/video-edit</code> protected X-Internal-Key:</p><ul><li>POST <code>/plan</code> accepts source envelope below; returns202 <code>{job_id,status,stage}</code> immediately, before probe/ASR/Claude. Cached by stable job ID+fingerprint. GET <code>/plans/{job_id}</code> returns stage and completed <code>{job_id,summary,plan}</code> or explicit FAILED/RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED. Persist provider_started before Claude; a crashed/unknown provider call must not automatically invoke Claude again. Worker startup resumes deterministic pre-provider work; ambiguous paid provider outcome requires reconciliation.</li><li>POST <code>/jobs</code> accepts same source envelope plus approved <code>plan</code>; returns202 <code>{job_id,status,stage}</code>. Same job+same payload replays; changed input409.</li><li>GET <code>/jobs/{job_id}</code> returns status/stage/progress/error and completed output receipt <code>{output_asset_id,sha256,size_bytes,mime_type,qc}</code> internally only.</li><li>GET <code>/capabilities</code> reports missing tool/model/provider readiness without spending API credit.</li></ul><p>Source envelope (snake_case): <code>{job_id,workspace_id,owner_id,project_id,base_revision,instruction,snapshot,sources:[{asset_id,kind,sha256,size_bytes,mime_type,metadata}]}</code>. IDs UUID. <code>kind</code> video/image/audio. Sources come only from private READY immutable project assets; max20 assets,128MiB each/512MiB total. Worker has configured Business API base only, no caller URL/path/object_key inputs. Download fixed internal <code>/api/v1/internal/video-edits/{job_id}/sources/{asset_id}</code> with internal auth; Business checks private job source allowlist and streams verified/decrypted source. Download verifies size+SHA before decoder/model. Source bytes/keys/credentials never enter the LLM prompt; bounded sampled frames and transcript plus selected metadata may.</p><p>Output transport: worker POST fixed internal <code>/api/v1/internal/video-edits/{job_id}/output-session</code> with <code>{fileName,contentType,sizeBytes,sha256,metadata}</code>; Business allocates deterministic output asset ID and existing private media quota/session/capability. Output is limited to128MiB. Worker PUTs the server-issued upload link (only configured Business origin or explicitly configured gateway origin, or HTTPS storage host), then POSTs <code>/output-complete</code> with <code>{sessionId}</code>; <code>/output-abort</code> on known pre-copy failures. Complete returns <code>{output_asset_id,sha256,size_bytes,mime_type}</code>. Business output stays a separate READY private asset, does not overwrite snapshot or originals. All internal routes require existing internal key using constant-time comparison and job ownership-derived scope, no actor chosen by caller. Worker never needs storage/AES secrets. Pending output publication is idempotent, including lost session-creation acknowledgments; reuse verified render artifact/hash across recovery.</p><p>Revision rule: validate the expected revision on first admission, then persist the canonical immutable snapshot/source allowlist. A later manual revision does not cancel or overwrite this separate output branch. Same-key retries return the original job before checking the latest revision; a changed request with that key conflicts.</p><p>Worker plan model is shared Python schema with strict bounded types, finite frame/timing/geometry and known asset IDs. Scope is the active scene; native time is120000ticks/second, distinguish source span from retimed timeline duration. Explicitly reject unsupported active-scene elements/effects rather than silently dropping manual edits. Exact plan is persisted and rendered; LLM-generated commands/filters/code are never executed. Initial output max120s,24/30fps,&lt;=1080x1920 or1920x1080. Render deadline600s, one running renderer per worker by default, bounded queue, durable Mongo job receipts/leases. Worker restart resumes safe unfinished jobs without another Claude/payment call. Output media namespace/quota are server-derived through Business. Failed partial uploads do not become completed receipts. QC: exact integer frame count, duration tolerance&lt;=1frame, dimensions/fps match plan, full decode succeeds, audio peak&lt;=0dBFS, integrated loudness measured/reported (voice master target-16±2LUFS when non-silent); no unmeasured quality-success claim.</p><h2 id="ui-and-error-states" tabindex="-1">UI and error states <a class="header-anchor" href="#ui-and-error-states" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UI and error states&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Use current native assistant drawer, one instruction field and a distinct automatic server render button. Show analyzing/planning/rendering/QC/upload/completed/failed and download; user may close browser and check saved server jobs. Do not silently replace local project. New text keys parallel in native <code>studio-messages.ts</code> vi/en; reuse theme tokens and accessible keyboard/focus controls. Host bridge exact selected-project POST and owner-scoped GET only; no arbitrary authenticated proxy.</p><h2 id="deployment-and-limits" tabindex="-1">Deployment and limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#deployment-and-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Deployment and limits&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Ship Dockerfile/compose+env.example and resource preflight for worker, data/scratch/model volumes, healthcheck and API URL settings. No actual VM exists in session. Verify locally and build container when available; distinguish packaged/tested from deployed. Continue to use external image+prompt generator for new footage; this runtime edits supplied/generated media. No crawling, automatic publishing, arbitrary web downloads, credit migration, manual-draft overwrite or model-selected shell execution.</p><h2 id="done" tabindex="-1">Done <a class="header-anchor" href="#done" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Done&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Feature docs first, reproducible tests, actual rendered fixture/QC, API owner/idempotency tests, host/native checks and build, progress/download browser proof. Preserve dirty baselines and leave changes uncommitted. Report executable capabilities and remaining configuration limits explicitly.</p><h2 id="_2026-11-11-—-editable-claude-chat-results" tabindex="-1">2026-11-11 — Editable Claude chat results <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-11-—-editable-claude-chat-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-11 — Editable Claude chat results&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Continuation of Claude chat “Tiếp tục công việc từ Codex”: the user requests sound, text and other edited components separately when applying a result to the workspace timeline. Preserve the MP4 preview/download and add a new scene with one-step Undo, without modifying the current scene. New Claude edits must also export TIMELINE.json using the existing RenderPlan schema, original canonical asset IDs and bundled music/SFX; original video audio becomes its own audio track. Text remains editable. Worker validates geometry, bounds, ownership and audio library names before marking a plan editable. Old one-clip geometry envelopes default to editable=false and continue to import their MP4; never pretend those are separated. Do not infer layers from an already flattened MP4. The local authenticated Claude CLI workflow already authorized in this conversation supersedes the older no-model-code description above; keep its existing 15-minute limit. Unsupported native effects must be disclosed alongside the result and after import. Custom newly generated media requires a future owned-asset transport and cannot be referenced by local path/URL. Missing/invalid requested sidecars must never be treated as editable. VI/EN strings remain parallel in studio-messages.ts and use existing theme, buttons and live status. Save failure is visible while retaining the undoable local scene.</p><h2 id="_2026-11-11-—-missing-editor-resources" tabindex="-1">2026-11-11 — Missing editor resources <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-11-—-missing-editor-resources" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-11 — Missing editor resources&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Fix requested missing color filters, uploaded audio and effect data. Audio means uploaded audio files do not appear in the Audio tab (user clarified); preserve sound in videos. Audio must list current project uploaded files, preview, import, search and add to timeline using existing media IDs. Filters/effects must have bundled working previews and useful supported presets, real renderer passes, editable parameters and Undo. Preserve existing design/storage/sync and parallel VI/EN labels. No paid calls or new rendering engine.</p>',25)])])}const h=t(r,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,h as default};
